9. Security Considerations
Allow only the services required by the system.
Restrict SSH access to trusted sources when possible.
Review existing firewall rules before making changes.
Test firewall behavior in an authorized environment.
Do not treat configured rules as proof of successful end-to-end filtering without appropriate testing.
10. Conclusion

UFW was installed and configured on Kali Linux. The default incoming policy was set to deny, while outgoing traffic was allowed. Additional rules were configured to permit SSH and HTTPS, deny HTTP, and block traffic from an example source IP address.

This task demonstrates basic Linux firewall administration, rule configuration, automation with Bash, and verification of firewall status. Further network testing can provide additional evidence that the rules behave as intended.

